cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "NEXUS: a compiler, CPU simulators, parallel, vector and GPU models and a Verilog MIPS CPU covering six computer-systems courses"
type: software
version: 3.0.0
authors:
  - given-names: "George David"
    family-names: "Tsitlauri"
    affiliation: "Department of Informatics and Telecommunications, University of Thessaly, Greece"
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gdtsitlauri/nexus-platform"
abstract: >-
  Supporting material for six computer-systems courses, as executable and tested C++20 and Verilog code:
  a NexusLang-to-MIPS compiler with linear-scan register allocation, attribute grammars, SSA/SCCP, loop
  unrolling and polyhedral transformations by integer linear programming; automata, LL/LR/Earley parsing and
  Hindley-Milner type inference; ISA styles and bit-exact IEEE-754 soft float; MIPS execution models from a
  functional interpreter to a Tomasulo core with reorder buffer, software pipelining by modulo scheduling,
  coarse-grained, fine-grained and simultaneous multithreading, multicore, network-on-chip, vector and SIMT
  GPU models; and a synthesisable 5-stage pipelined MIPS core with memory-mapped I/O and interrupts,
  co-simulated against the simulators.
keywords: [compilers, computer architecture, MIPS, simulation, Tomasulo, polyhedral, linear programming, software pipelining, multithreading, vector processors, Verilog, education]
